{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/403753-contracts-from-durance","id":403753,"title":"Contracts from Durance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-12T15:33:49-08:00","id":403753,"title":"Contracts from Durance","content":"My character for an upcoming campaign spent her time in Arcadia playing through Cliff Hanger, Cobra Command, Dragon's Lair and other laserdisc games of the 1980s. From the inside. As the main character, but without the benefit of transitions and scene jumps, or extra lives. Get killed in a particular game, start over. And she had to worry about food, water, sleep and hygiene. She's a Bloodbrute Ogre, not surprisingly. She has to have Seven League Stride (I think that's the name) for some scenes in Time Gal and Cliff Hanger, but beyond that I'm not too sure what to give the girl. The ST uses a house rule for chargen: you start with five dots' worth of clauses, but each clause is bought individually (buying the second dot in a contract doesn't automatically give you the first, for example). I think that rule was intended to make goblin contracts and regular contracts cost-balanced at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 02-12-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T23:54:25-08:00","id":404180,"title":"","content":"Basically any clause from Contracts of the Board sound right up the character's alley.<br /> <br /> Hearth is just so down right useful I can't imagine her not wanting it. Especially in a game environment the hero's seem to have impossible luck. Though for her that might just be because of having to reload every time.<br /> <br /> Stone: Orge's Rending Grasp would fit if she eventually started to go off script and just tearing down the dungeons. She could have learned Gluttonous Feast of Health to turn those dead enemies into health levels.<br /> <br /> Den: First couple of clauses offer good shelter/survival abilities.<br /> <br /> Eternal Autumn: Last Breath Issac for food.<br /> <br /> Eternal Spring: Gift of Warm Breath for not having to eat, drink, or sleep. Warmth of Blood for more heals<br /> <br /> For more item based gaming see Animation (Knowing Touch and Instant Expertise) and Artifice (all clauses) for glitching broken items back to working, sundering weapons, looking at item stats, or finding cheat codes that increase weapon damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}